«
@@ ============================================================
@@ WPNext — where is the next waypoint, and how far off the route am I?
@@
@@ Input : φ λ GS — present latitude and longitude (East positive), and
@@         ground speed. Plain numbers are degrees and knots; values
@@         with a unit are accepted. GS = 0 skips the time estimate.
@@ Output: tagged values — To: the next waypoint, Brg: its true
@@         bearing, Dist: its distance (nmi), XTD: the cross-track
@@         distance from the active leg, positive right of it (nmi),
@@         and ETE: the time to reach it at GS (h.mmss).
@@
@@ The active leg, from waypoint RouteLeg to the next one, starts at 1.
@@ When the present position is abeam or past the end of the leg, the
@@ next leg becomes active, and the results refer to it.
@@ Bearings and distances come from VincentyInv (WGS-84); the cross-
@@ and along-track distances use a sphere of the mean radius,
@@ 6 371 008.8 m, largely accurate at the scale of a leg.
@@ The angle mode and the angle units setting are restored.
@@ ============================================================

  IF DUP TypeName "unit" ≠ THEN 1_knot * END
  'Route' RCL
  IFERR 'RouteLeg' RCL THEN DROP 1 END
  'AngleMode' RCL 'SetAngleUnits' RCL
  RAD NoAngleUnits
  → pp lp gs rtl leg amode aunits
  «
    @ Advance past the legs whose end is already abeam or behind
    WHILE
      rtl leg GET LIST→ DROP rtl leg 1 + GET LIST→ DROP
      → na pa la nb pb lb
      «
        pa la pb lb ⓁVincentyInv DROP
        pa la pp lp ⓁVincentyInv DROP
        → dab cab dap cap
        «
          dap UVAL 6371008.8 /
          cap cab - 1_r CONVERT UVAL
          → tap dcr
          «
            '6371008.8*ACOS(COS(tap)/COS(ASIN(SIN(tap)*SIN(dcr))))' EVAL
            dab UVAL ≥
          »
        »
      »
      leg rtl SIZE 1 - < AND
    REPEAT
      leg 1 + 'leg' STO
    END
    leg 'RouteLeg' STO

    rtl leg GET LIST→ DROP rtl leg 1 + GET LIST→ DROP
    → na pa la nb pb lb
    «
      pp lp pb lb ⓁVincentyInv DROP
      pa la pb lb ⓁVincentyInv DROP
      pa la pp lp ⓁVincentyInv DROP
      → dist brg dab cab dap cap
      «
        dap UVAL 6371008.8 /
        cap cab - 1_r CONVERT UVAL
        → tap dcr
        «
          nb "To" →TAG
          brg "Brg" →TAG
          dist 1_nmi CONVERT "Dist" →TAG
          '6371008.8*ASIN(SIN(tap)*SIN(dcr))' EVAL
          1_m * 1_nmi CONVERT "XTD" →TAG
          IF gs UVAL 0 > THEN
            dist gs / 1_h CONVERT UVAL →HMS "ETE" →TAG
          END
        »
      »
    »
    amode EVAL IF aunits THEN SetAngleUnits ELSE NoAngleUnits END
  »
»
